text:
Opening the native phone dialer without showing other installed dialers

### Use case

I want to open native phone call dialer with out showing other options. the current url_launcher package failed to provide such functionality. here is snippet code I am using.
Future<void> _launchShortCode(BuildContext context) async {
final phoneLaunchUri = Uri(
scheme: 'tel',
path: '888',
);

try {
if (!await launchUrl(phoneLaunchUri)) {
if (context.mounted) {
_showErrorDialog(context, 'Could not launch phone app');
}
}
} catch (e) {
debugPrint('Error launching phone: $e');
if (context.mounted) {
_showErrorDialog(context, 'Error launching phone');
}
}
}

### Proposal

This is package related.

vscode.workspace.onDidChangeConfiguration not called on theme changes

Type: Bug

With this trivial extension:

export function activate(context: vscode.ExtensionContext) {
context.subscriptions.push(vscode.workspace.onDidChangeConfiguration(event => {
if (event.affectsConfiguration("workbench.iconTheme"))
console.log('theme changed');
}));
}

If the File Icon Theme is changed from the File menu, the event is not triggered.
If the File Icon Theme is changed from the settings view, the event is triggered.

VS Code version: Code 1.95.0 (912bb683695358a54ae0c670461738984cbb5b95, 2024-10-28T20:16:24.561Z)
